WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.957
Your home has a loan for twenty or thirty years.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.148
If your income stopped tomorrow, who would pay the instalment?

3
00:00:08.248 --> 00:00:11.811
For a mortgage, the bank usually asks for life cover assigned to it,

4
00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:14.261
and home insurance against fire and earthquake.

5
00:00:14.564 --> 00:00:17.001
You can buy them from an insurer you choose,

6
00:00:17.095 --> 00:00:19.358
as long as the cover is equivalent.

7
00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:23.650
But the cover the bank asks for pays off the loan.

8
00:00:23.895 --> 00:00:27.760
The home is debt-free, but the family still has bills every month.

9
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.101
Check three points:

10
00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:34.699
whether the cover reaches the whole balance, whether both borrowers are insured,

11
00:00:34.793 --> 00:00:37.857
and whether there is cover for permanent total disability.

12
00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:43.499
A serious illness can stop your income without triggering life cover.

13
00:00:44.599 --> 00:00:48.569
Decreasing cover goes down with the balance and usually costs less.

14
00:00:48.941 --> 00:00:52.307
Level cover stays the same, and as the loan shrinks,

15
00:00:52.331 --> 00:00:55.105
whatever is left over goes to your family.

16
00:00:56.205 --> 00:00:58.131
And do not forget the home itself:

17
00:00:58.318 --> 00:01:01.103
cover for fire, earthquake and flood,

18
00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:03.913
for a sum that matches today’s rebuilding cost.

19
00:01:04.286 --> 00:01:08.906
From 2026, premiums for natural-disaster cover are deductible from

20
00:01:08.906 --> 00:01:13.816
taxable income up to five hundred euros, where the conditions are met.

21
00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:18.723
Check your loan protection with the free tool on avrastro.com,

22
00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:20.871
and go through it with an advisor.
